# Line endings: LF, everywhere, on every platform.
#
# Two things in this repository are line-ending sensitive. The built-in chat
# templates and their .json companions under
# src/CodeBrix.Ollama.ModelRunner/Templates/OllamaGo/BuiltIn/ are embedded
# resources, so whatever bytes are on disk at pack time ship inside the assembly;
# and the ModelRunner test suite compares rendered templates and generated
# grammars with its fixture files byte for byte. A checkout that expanded LF to
# CRLF (core.autocrlf=true on Windows) would fail that suite and would pack CRLF
# templates into the NuGet package for every consumer, on every platform.
#
# The committed blobs are already LF. These rules only stop a checkout from
# changing them, which also keeps the vendored llama.cpp snapshot under
# llama-native-tools/llama.cpp/ byte-identical to upstream.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touched. A native library, a model file or an image with newline
# translation applied to it is silently corrupt, so these are declared rather
# than left to git's heuristic.
*.gguf  binary
*.png   binary
*.dylib binary
*.so    binary
*.dll   binary
*.pdb   binary
*.xz    binary
